  "question": {
    "text": "If $\\frac{\\pi}{2} \\leq x \\leq \\frac{3 \\pi}{4}$, then $\\cos ^{-1}\\left(\\frac{12}{13} \\cos x+\\frac{5}{13} \\sin x\\right)$ is equal to",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "UiS2a",
      "text": "$x-\\tan ^{-1} \\frac{4}{3}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "kToFg",
      "text": "$x+\\tan ^{-1} \\frac{4}{5}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "CDr52",
      "text": "$x-\\tan ^{-1} \\frac{5}{12}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "mxDQ0",
      "text": "$x+\\tan ^{-1} \\frac{5}{12}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & \\frac{12}{13} \\cos x+\\frac{5}{13} \\sin x \\\\ & \\text { Let } \\tan \\alpha=\\frac{5}{12}, \\alpha \\in\\left(0, \\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right) \\\\ & \\Rightarrow \\sin \\alpha=\\frac{5}{13}, \\cos \\alpha=\\frac{12}{13}\\end{aligned}$\n$\\begin{aligned} & \\Rightarrow \\frac{12}{13} \\cos x+\\frac{5}{13} \\sin x=\\cos \\alpha \\cos x+\\sin \\alpha \\sin x \\\\ & \\quad=\\cos (x-\\alpha) \\\\ & \\Rightarrow \\cos ^{-1}[\\cos (x-\\alpha)]=x-\\alpha \\\\ & \\quad=x-\\tan ^{-1}\\left(\\frac{5}{12}\\right)\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
